 ```
 
+Adding a method that is already supported is a no-op, as long as the `hasBody`
+option matches the current body support of that method. Otherwise, an
+`FST_ERR_ROUTE_METHOD_ALREADY_SUPPORTED` error is thrown, so that the standard
+HTTP methods are not silently overridden:
+
+```js
+// Throws: GET is supported without a body
+fastify.addHttpMethod('GET', { hasBody: true })
+```
+
+To change the body support of an already supported method, the `override`
+option must be set explicitly:
+
+```js
+fastify.addHttpMethod('GET', { hasBody: true, override: true })
+```
+
 > ⚠ Warning:
-> `addHttpMethod` overrides existing methods.
+> Overriding a standard HTTP method may break plugins and clients that expect
+> the default behavior.
 
 #### addSchema
 <a id="add-schema"></a>
